    "answer_baseline": "Based on the provided context:\n\n* **Wholly State-funded institutions:** No religious instruction is allowed in any educational institution that is wholly maintained out of State funds [Article 28(1)]. \n* **State-administered institutions established under a trust/endowment:** Religious instruction is permitted if the institution is administered by the State but was established under an endowment or trust that requires religious instruction to be imparted [Article 28(2)].\n* **State-aided or recognized institutions:** Religious instruction may be imparted, but no person attending an institution receiving aid out of State funds (or recognized by the State) can be required to participate in it unless they (or their guardian, if a minor) give their consent [Article 28(3)].",
